{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GDdKCLPtcvDb43ueKqyp1r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's a difference! GNU gdircolors reports ALL errors in the database, not just the first one:\n\n```\n--- Multiple errors in database ---\ngdircolors: -:1: invalid line;  missing second token\ngdircolors: -:2: invalid line;  missing second token\nexit: 1\n```\n\nBut our binary stops at the first error:\n\n```\n--- Multiple errors in database ---\ndircolors: -:1: invalid line;  missing second token\nexit: 1\n```\n\nThis is a real difference in R3.4 behavior: \"Must print a diagnostic to stderr for each error including the filename and line number of the offending line in the database.\"\n\n\nThe spec is clear that we need to report every error, not stop after the first one. GNU gdircolors keeps parsing through the entire file and collects all the issues before exiting. I should also look for any other edge cases where our implementation might diverge from the expected behavior.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1429,"cache_read_input_tokens":36066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1429},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00a7fe6e-2e16-4c02-acf2-f923819546ce","uuid":"24437ef4-fc7b-4968-9ebe-f92b90e29458"}
